{
  "task.79BBB59F2FD756F8.title": "Deep Strains",
  "quest.3C58133AB9909BC3.title": "&2Bacterial Fuel Cell",
  "quest.7E24BA960EFA7931.quest_desc": [
    "Salt Water on its own does nothing. The &aMixer&r turns it into the chemicals the rest of the mod runs on.",
    "",
    "Build a &aMixer&r and give it a beam of at least 10 AP. Fill its input tank with Salt Water, add the ingredients &eJEI&r lists, and it makes &bEAS&r, Etching Acid or Aquarine Steel Compound, five compound from two Raw Iron.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "You will need a &2Whisk&r to build one, repaired from the Broken Whisks that Drowned sometimes drop.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: a recipe only starts when its result fits, and while the output tank holds fluid a bucket empties that tank instead of filling the input. Empty the output between batches.",
  ],
  "quest.5F23221A22811049.quest_desc": [
    "The hull has nine module slots that add sonar, speed, weapons and more.",
    "",
    "Start with a &aSonar Module&r. Each ping outlines every ore vein within 48 blocks and every hostile within 32, straight through rock, and gives the crew night vision.",
    "",
    "Right-click the hull from outside with a wrench to open the module bay. Passive modules work from any slot, and a second copy of one adds nothing.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"While you pilot, the modules replace your hotbar. Pick one with the number keys or the scroll wheel, then fire it with \", {\"keybind\": \"key.attack\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: Left Button\"}}, \" or \", {\"keybind\": \"key.nautec.submarine_ability\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: F\"}}, \".\"]",
  ],
  "quest.2392DE947119DD60.title": "&3Solar Module",
  "quest.66A97821D6355722.quest_desc": [
    "One crafted part does two jobs.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aBuoyancy Tank&r. Fitted in the Body slot it lets you fly the way you do in creative mode, in water or out of it.",
    "",
    "Keep a second one for the Sea Scout, whose hull is built around a tank along with a Prismatic Battery and an Eldritch Heart.",
  ],
  "quest.3110B6A87C933A2D.title": "&2Grafting Station",
  "quest.0F4B9E3D2B15A9C8.title": "&bFiring Your First Beam",
  "quest.57A356FE9F206C33.quest_desc": [
    "Murky brown water over basalt and magma, with bubbles rising all the time and visibility down to about fifty blocks.",
    "",
    "Shear a &aVent Tubeworm&r from the floor of the &bHydrothermal Vents&r.",
    "",
    "The magma here makes bubble columns, which fill Glass Bottles with pressurized air for your diving tank. Vent Crawlers walk the floor.",
  ],
  "quest.3EAD190846D5F280.quest_desc": [
    "A capped Lithophiles colony fills its 64-item output slot in under half a minute, and a full slot pauses that colony.",
    "",
    "Pull the output out with item pipes or plenty of hoppers. One Hopper moves 150 items a minute, and an upgraded Industrial Bio Reactor makes thousands a minute.",
    "",
    "Hoppers under any block of the floor and a pipe on the front of the controller both take from the output slots and nothing else. Item pipes from mods such as &ePipez&r keep up far better than hoppers.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: a paused colony makes nothing, but it does not age or shrink either, so a backed-up line costs you output, never colonies.",
  ],
  "quest.49C42EC7FAC6095B.quest_desc": [
    "&aRusty Crates&r sit at the foot of every &6Nautec Ruin&r, and plain Crates turn up in shipwreck and ruin chests.",
    "",
    "Bring home a &aRusty Crate&r. Breaking a crate drops it with its loot still inside, so you can carry it away before opening it.",
    "",
    "A plain Crate opens like a chest. A Rusty Crate is rusted shut until you etch it clean, and it holds better salvage than a plain one.",
  ],
  "quest.5274AC4F7E7C6369.title": "&aElectrolyte Algae Serum",
  "quest.30A058E82CF6766A.quest_desc": [
    "Swimming gets slow once your builds are spread across the sea floor.",
    "",
    "Make a &aWave Jet&r, get into water and hold right-click. It pulls you wherever you look at about twice your swimming speed, and while you thrust your air bar stops draining. It takes both hands.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"It runs on its own 6,000 AP cell, which you fill on the Charger. With your head above water it skims along the surface instead of launching you out, and \", {\"keybind\": \"key.nautec.wave_jet_light\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: F\"}}, \" switches its spotlight on and off.\"]",
  ],
  "task.53CA5CD95643AAB1.title": "&eObserve&r: Prismarine Crystal Part",
  "quest.0F4B9E3D2B15A9C8.quest_desc": [
    "An &2Aquatic Catalyst&r burns prismarine and fires the power out as a beam, but only into a block that can take it.",
    "",
    "Make some &aPrismarine Laser Relays&r and point your catalyst at one. A relay takes the beam in at its back and sends it on from its front for another 16 blocks, with nothing lost on the way.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Load the catalyst by right-clicking it with fuel, or feed it from a hopper. Prismarine Shards burn at purity 0.4, Prismarine Crystals at 0.8 and Prismarine Crystal Shards at 1.2, and it moves straight from one item to the next, so the beam never flickers while the stack lasts.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the face you look at while placing the catalyst becomes its pale intake. The beam leaves from the dark face with the cyan lens on the opposite side, and fuel only burns while a receiver sits on that side.",
  ],
  "quest.5274AC4F7E7C6369.quest_desc": [
    "The Mixer's most useful product is &bElectrolyte Algae Serum&r, or EAS.",
    "",
    "Mix an &aEAS Bucket&r and bottle some of it into EAS Vials. You will want a bucket for the Mutator and vials for the Syringe Robot Arm.",
    "",
    "Pour EAS out as a source block and drop an Aquarine Steel tool into it. After 7.5 seconds the tool's ability is unlocked for good and the source is used up, so one bucket infuses one tool.",
  ],
  "quest.6CC5E95BCA30A555.title": "&bCopy and Paste",
  "task.55E76BF26C538E0D.title": "Item Transformation",
  "quest.237CBF1B089BC523.quest_desc": [
    "Before the laser machines you need a cheap, tough metal for rods, tools and frames.",
    "",
    "Smelt Cast Iron Compound into &aCast Iron Ingots&r and turn a couple into rods. The Grafting Tool is made from them.",
    "",
    "A Blast Furnace smelts the compound twice as fast. Anchors and Oil Barrels from the sea floor blast down into cast iron too, and the nuggets repair a Broken Whisk later on.",
  ],
  "quest.4EAA319397136532.title": "&aEtching Acid",
  "task.10D39D02D2B6FDD2.title": "Lithophiles",
  "quest.65E1AE8CEB6387FD.title": "&dAtlantean Rifle",
  "quest.0DC9E401CA949038.quest_desc": [
    "With power to spare, a reactor can turn AP into output.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aReactor Speed Upgrade&r and put it in a reactor's upgrade slot. Each one adds 50% production speed to every colony in the reactor and multiplies its power draw by 1.6.",
    "",
    "Faster colonies also spend fewer nutrients per item, since the buffer drains per tick of work. Two of them raise a full Bio Reactor's draw from 100 AP to 256. A beam stronger than that draw speeds the reactor up again, multiplied with the upgrades.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"All three upgrades are built on \", {\"text\": \"Deep Steel Plating\", \"color\": \"dark_green\"}, \" from \", {\"text\": \"Pressing the Deep\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"684644505C6D47D4\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to Pressing the Deep Quest\"}}, \".\"]",
  ],
  "quest.71F0F2A1ED30A94A.title": "&bLucky Zones",
  "quest.327AC224CD74178C.title": "&bStacking the Odds",
  "quest.3B7FCE8FEC7A4C26.title": "&dAddressing a Network",
  "quest.51EC17DA8C101A1E.quest_desc": [
    "The chain keeps going past iron.",
    "",
    "Mutate &bFerrophiles&r with a Gold Ingot to get &bAurrophiles&r, which make Gold Ingots and feed on Gold Ore.",
    "",
    "A success uses up the whole input colony, so split off or keep back a working Ferrophiles colony before you mutate it.",
  ],
  "quest.160787EC65DDE421.quest_desc": [
    "Every uplink on a network pools its power in orbit. A &aResonance Node&r draws on that pool from wherever you place it.",
    "",
    "Join it to the network the same way as a pylon. Set to Input, it takes beams fired into any side and FE from cables and sends both up to the uplink. Set to Output, it fires the AP back out of its crystal tip as a beam and pushes the FE into anything touching it.",
    "",
    "Output nodes share the network's power with downlinks and charms by priority, and each node has its own limit, both set at the top of its screen. In a dimension with no uplink of its own, its beam arrives with 5% less purity.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the network needs an Uplink Array with a launched satellite somewhere, or a node has nothing to connect to.",
  ],
  "quest.2CDD35D21A370805.quest_desc": [
    "One catalyst sends 12 AP per tick at most, and plenty of machines want more than that.",
    "",
    "Make a &aLaser Junction&r and an &2Aquarine Steel Wrench&r. Right-click a junction face with the wrench to make it an input, or Sneak + Right-click to make it an output. Every input adds together, so two catalysts into one junction give you 24 AP.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The total is split evenly across the connected outputs, and the purity coming out is the average of the inputs. A source that has run dry counts as zero, so keep every input fed.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click the air to switch the wrench between Rotate, Item Sides and Fluid Sides. Rotate turns any block with a facing, and the Sides modes set what hoppers and pipes can do through each face of a machine. Junction faces, multiblocks and laser ports work in every mode, so keep it on your hotbar.",
  ],
  "quest.1D7AAD2487528786.title": "&5Resonant Shards",
  "quest.217D267D6A62F48D.title": "&5Atlantean Pressure Synthesizer",
  "quest.55D7BD0D53341399.quest_desc": [
    "A beam looks the same whether it carries 2 AP or 200, which makes a stalled machine hard to diagnose.",
    "",
    "Make a &aPrism Monocle&r and wear it in your helmet slot or its own Monocle curio slot. Looking at any laser block then shows the power and purity arriving there.",
    "",
    "It also reads machine states, such as a Pressure Forge's acid level or a Gateway's address, and it clears underwater fog the same way a Diving Helmet does.",
  ],
  "task.7BE02BF2C1DB445C.title": "Piloting",
  "quest.027581A4ED726B8B.quest_desc": [
    "With EAS on hand you can make tools that run on AP and carry an ability each.",
    "",
    "Make an &aAquarine Steel Pickaxe&r and a matching sword, then infuse them in an EAS source. Sneak + Right-click an infused tool to switch its ability on or off.",
    "",
    "They never break. Each block mined or mob hit costs AP instead, 1,200 to a full tool, topped up on the Charger or by the Battery. The pickaxe mines a 3 by 3 face and is the only tool that chips shards off a Prismarine Crystal, and the sword calls lightning on what it hits.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: the lightning also strikes anything within a few blocks of the target, you included.",
  ],
  "quest.07ACFFA6F8A00E9C.title": "&2Bacteria",
  "quest.65C5C6A7BE9AC4E6.quest_desc": [
    "Once you would rather build than sit holding a rod, let a machine do the fishing.",
    "",
    "Place a &aFishing Station&r over open water and aim a beam into its top or bottom. Any amount of power runs it, and it rolls ordinary fishing loot every two seconds into 15 slots.",
    "",
    "Every block in the 5 by 5 area under it, two blocks deep, has to be plain water. Kelp, seagrass, waterlogged blocks or Salt Water anywhere in that area stop it.",
  ],
  "quest.0F1BF451F6A84E98.quest_desc": [
    "Past a certain depth a diving suit stops being enough.",
    "",
    "Build a &aSea Scout&r, a two seat submarine that keeps its crew breathing and takes the hits for them. Use the item while looking at open water to launch it, then right-click the hull to board. The first person aboard pilots.",
    "",
    "It runs everything from one 1,000,000 AP cell and has 80 hull points and nine module slots. Sneak + Right-click an empty hull to pick it back up with its charge, damage and modules intact.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the hull is built around a Prismatic Battery, an Eldritch Heart and a Buoyancy Tank, so this quest opens once you have the first two.",
  ],
  "quest.40653ACDABFB5BE1.title": "&bStronger Beams",
  "quest.2271043535B4D61D.quest_desc": [
    "Feed a &aPrismatic Emitter&r FE from a cable or a receiving pylon, and it hands that power to machines nearby without a single wire.",
    "",
    "Right-click the emitter with the &aTuning Fork&r to tune it, then right-click each machine to link it. One emitter reaches 16 blocks, feeds up to 16 machines and shares 10,000 FE/t between them with no loss.",
    "",
    "A tuned fork links another emitter the same way, so power hops from emitter to emitter to reach machines further away. Sneak + Right-click the air to tune the fork to a different emitter, or Sneak + Right-click the emitter to unlink everything.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: only the player who placed an emitter can tune a fork to it.",
  ],
  "quest.1FA84DC387722607.quest_desc": [
    "The Fusion Plant is a sealed chamber around a cultivated crystal, and its shell takes several new blocks:",
    "- &aFusion Casing&r: every edge of the chamber, and any wall block you like.",
    "- &aAquamarine Structural Glass&r: filler for the walls, floor and ceiling.",
    "- &aFusion Collector&r: one in the center of the ceiling and one in the center of the floor, in line with the crystal.",
    "- &aLaser Injector&r: one to four, each in the middle of a side wall at the height of the crystal's core, facing it.",
    "- &aContainment Coil&r: an optional wall block that raises the output cap.",
    "- &aFusion Port&r: an optional wall block that takes Salt Water in and pushes FE out.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The crystal stands on the floor inside, and its core is the fourth block up. Inside, the chamber is 6 blocks tall and 3, 5, 7 or 9 blocks wide and deep, with the crystal in the middle.",
    "",
    "Leave only air or water inside. You can build the whole thing underwater.",
  ],
  "quest.0EEFEF7693B5FC78.quest_desc": [
    "A spawner left alone fills a room with mobs. A confined one keeps them in the cage and hands you their drops instead.",
    "",
    "Use a &2Spawner Confinement Matrix&r on a mob spawner to turn it into a &aConfined Spawner&r, then aim a laser beam into any face. It spends 50 AP each tick while it runs and rolls the mob's loot once for every mob it would have spawned, counted as a player kill.",
    "",
    "Drops fill its 54 slots and experience fills a 16,000 mB tank, and pipes can pull both out. Mined with a pickaxe, it keeps its mob, filter, drops and experience. Empty it, then Sneak + use it with an empty hand to release the spawner exactly as it was.",
  ],
  "quest.6DBCA290A9EAB706.quest_desc": [
    "A bare tap moves 8 items a second, plus 1,000 mB of fluid and 5,000 FE each tick, on every face.",
    "",
    "Put an &aEddy Upgrade&r in the tap's upgrade slot to speed up all of its faces at once. Each tier is crafted from the one before it: Surge adds an emerald, Riptide a diamond and Maelstrom a Flawless Prismarine Crystal.",
    "",
    "A Maelstrom tap moves 64 items every tick, plus 1,000,000 mB and 5,000,000 FE each tick, on every face.",
  ],
  "quest.684644505C6D47D4.quest_desc": [
    "The Forge makes two things nothing else can.",
    "",
    "Press a &aFlawless Prismarine Crystal&r from a Resonant Shard and some &2Deep Steel Plating&r from an Aquarine Steel Ingot.",
    "",
    "The crystal needs purity 2.0 with the Forge at Y -20 or lower. The plating needs purity 2.5 at Y -40 or lower, which is why the Abyssal Trench is the place to build.",
    "",
    "Both go into Neptune's Trident and the Atlantean Rifle, and the plating is also what repairs a breached Sea Scout on an anvil.",
  ],
  "quest.404A544FCA60A839.title": "&2Opening the Roof",
  "task.1B98D41FDC2E5C7D.title": "Live Catches",
  "quest.25F78E2C1065E392.quest_desc": [
    "Gems come next.",
    "",
    "Mutate &bAurrophiles&r with a Diamond to get &bAdamantophiles&r, which make Diamonds and feed on Diamond Ore.",
    "",
    "Diamonds come slowly. The strain's Strain Yield is 0.12, so even a capped colony makes only about 16 a minute, and a gem farm needs more reactors than a metal one.",
  ],
  "quest.31895972F81D14AE.title": "&5Resonance Network",
  "quest.29685DB8EA94F30A.quest_desc": [
    "Every strain has a &bStrain Yield&r that scales how fast it works, and the valuable ones are slow.",
    "",
    "A colony at the stat caps (Production Rate 2, size 40,000) makes about 134 Stone a minute. An iron strain at the same stats makes about 81 ingots, gold 54, diamonds 16 and emeralds 13. Size counts too, since a tiny colony works at half the speed of a capped one.",
    "",
    "Plan around the item. Three capped Ferrophiles in a Bio Reactor make about 242 Iron Ingots a minute, while three capped Adamantophiles make about 48 Diamonds, so a gem farm needs about five times the reactors to match an iron farm.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Fresh colonies run at roughly a tenth of these numbers. The \", {\"text\": \"Production Rates\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:aquatic_biology/production_rates.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide lists every strain's Strain Yield.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.6C51CE5E6702F34F.quest_desc": [
    "Strains for other mods' metals and gems only exist when a mod in the pack adds that material.",
    "",
    "They come off the strains you already have, from Lithophiles for the common metals up to Aurrophiles and Adamantophiles for the rarest. Each eats and makes its own material.",
    "",
    "&eJEI&r's Bacteria Mutations and Bio Reactor categories show which ones this pack has.",
  ],
  "quest.4702ABE2F7F6FD31.title": "&2Making It Last",
  "task.54F29756F929C887.title": "Iron from a colony",
  "quest.2FD63A10FF3E5F24.title": "&5The Abyssal Trench",
  "quest.62D4AD580B20C416.quest_desc": [
    "The strains grafted from the Nautec oceans are ready to work in a Bio Reactor as soon as you have them:",
    "",
    "- &aHalotrophs&r: Deep Kelp in a Grove, makes Kelp.",
    "- &2Algaeformers&r: Luminescent Algae in a Grove, makes Seagrass.",
    "- &aPhototrophs&r: Prismarine Frond on a Reef, makes Sugar Cane.",
    "- &2Calciophiles&r: Abyssal Coral in a Trench, makes Bone Meal.",
    "- &aSulfurophiles&r: Vent Tubeworm at the Vents, makes Gunpowder.",
    "- &2Lithophiles&r: Budding Prismarine on a Reef, makes Stone.",
    "",
    "Lithophiles matters most. It is the parent of the metal strains, and grafting it skips a slow mutation from Thermophiles.",
  ],
  "quest.747774F0F1C5F3E3.title": "&2Surface Strains",
  "quest.53F8764099C14F93.title": "&dFusion Plant",
  "quest.3787C51DB72BF43D.quest_desc": [
    "The Forge only runs with eight blocks of water stacked above it, which rules out most of your base.",
    "",
    "Mix a &aPressure Synthesizer&r from a Flawless Prismarine Crystal and 8,000 mB of Salt Water, then right-click the Forge with it. It stands in for the water column, though the Forge still has to sit at Y 0 or lower and each recipe keeps its own maximum Y.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click the Forge with an empty hand to take it off again. A Prism Monocle shows which synthesizer is fitted.",
  ],
  "quest.0131C83A87A25AF4.title": "&2Bacterial Analyzer",
  "quest.6843F1AA23F6FFB4.quest_desc": [
    "Breeding a strong colony takes a long run of mutations, and at the end you have one of it.",
    "",
    "Build a &aColony Replicator&r. Put your best analyzed colony in the template slot and feed colonies of the same strain into the fodder slot, fresh grafts included. Every 20,000 biomass of fodder becomes one copy of the template, and the template is never used up.",
    "",
    "A copy can come out up to a tenth worse on a stat. &bMutation Resistance&r lowers that chance, and at the resistance cap every copy is perfect, so breed it up first. Splice mode crosses two colonies of the same strain and takes each stat from one parent, usually the better one.",
    "",
    "It needs a beam of 80 AP at purity 2.0 or more into any face except the front, and takes 30 seconds per colony on that beam, less on a stronger one. Copies start at a fresh graft's size, so grow them in the Incubator before putting them to work.",
  ],
  "quest.2DD115082017F9E3.quest_desc": [
    "&eNautec&r tools, armor and vehicles run on stored AP instead of durability, and something has to fill them.",
    "",
    "Build a &aCharger&r, set an item on it with a right-click and aim a beam at it. It charges at the beam's full power, so a stronger beam fills things faster.",
    "",
    "The &2Prismatic Battery&r holds 10,000 AP. Fill it on the Charger, Sneak + Right-click to switch it on and put it in your Curios Battery slot, and it tops up the powered items in your hotbar and inventory.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: armor you are wearing is outside the battery's reach, so charge it on the Charger.",
  ],
  "quest.2EAF6EB6688A64EB.quest_desc": [
    "Metallophiles has two side mutations worth having.",
    "",
    "Mutate it with Redstone for &bAcidophiles&r, which make Redstone, or with Lapis Lazuli for &bAzuritophiles&r, which make Lapis Lazuli. Each feeds on its own ore.",
  ],
  "quest.5085FC6585F588B9.quest_desc": [
    "The chance in &eJEI&r is the best case. Mutation Resistance lowers it, by half at the cap, and a colony at the 40,000 size cap has a quarter less.",
    "",
    "A failed attempt kills up to a quarter of the colony, less with Mutation Resistance, but it never takes the last of it, so the Mutator keeps trying.",
    "",
    "The new colony's size does not depend on the parent, so mutate while colonies are small and grow them afterwards. Each success moves Growth Rate and Production Rate by up to a tenth either way and Lifespan by up to 100 ticks. Hold Shift and Ctrl over an analyzed dish to see the ranges.",
  ],
  "quest.5E3EDE7F8AF2489A.title": "&6Vent Crawlers",
  "quest.53F8764099C14F93.quest_subtitle": "Nautec's Strongest Power Source",
  "quest.0F1BF451F6A84E98.title": "&3The Sea Scout",
  "quest.062E3FE8A6A3A450.title": "&2Combustion Dynamo",
  "quest.404A544FCA60A839.quest_desc": [
    "The finished frame does nothing until it is formed and fed power.",
    "",
    "Right-click the Industrial Bio Reactor with the &2Aquarine Steel Wrench&r, without sneaking, to form it. If a block is wrong, chat names its position, what is there and what should be.",
    "",
    "Then wrench any Aquarine Steel Block of the formed roof to turn it into a hatch. A hatch takes a beam pointing down into it, an edge hatch also takes one into its outer side, and every hatch's power adds up at the controller, so several small beams work as well as one big one.",
    "",
    "It needs 100 AP plus 50 per filled colony slot, 550 AP for nine colonies before upgrades, which six Energy Converters on six hatches cover. Keep hoppers off the hatches, since a block sitting on a hatch stops the beam coming in.",
  ],
  "quest.36E74E70F0ACCAD5.quest_desc": [
    "A Grafting Station turns out colonies faster than one Analyzer can read them.",
    "",
    "Craft an &aAdvanced Bacterial Analyzer&r. It analyzes nine dishes side by side, each in the same 60 ticks a single dish takes in the basic Analyzer.",
    "",
    "It needs a beam of at least 40 AP at purity 2.1, into any face except the front, so a Prismarine Crystal beam or a full purity Bacterial Fuel Cell runs it. Only unanalyzed dishes go in, so a pipe straight from a Grafting Station never clogs it.",
  ],
  "quest.29685DB8EA94F30A.title": "&2Strain Yield",
  "quest.77FFEC3A2289F5C2.quest_desc": [
    "The sea floor is scattered with old prismarine machinery, and some of it still works.",
    "",
    "&eNautec&r machines run on light instead of cables. Power is a &blaser beam&r fired from one block into another, and almost everything you build here needs a beam pointed at it.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Get an &aAquatic Catalyst&r, your first beam source. Every &6Nautec Ruin&r, a small dark prismarine arch on the ocean floor, has one seated in it, and mining it drops the block. You can also craft one from Polished Prismarine and Prismarine Crystals.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Craft the \", \"color\": \"gray\", \"italic\": true}, {\"text\": \"Nautec Guide\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"italic\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, {\"text\": \" from a Book and a Cast Iron Nugget for the full manual, or hover any Nautec item and hold \", \"color\": \"gray\", \"italic\": true}, {\"keybind\": \"key.guideme.guide\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"italic\": true, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: G\"}}, {\"text\": \" to open its page.\", \"color\": \"gray\", \"italic\": true}]",
  ],
  "quest.63177C0A3FA7720F.quest_desc": [
    "One module takes you home from anywhere.",
    "",
    "Fit a &aTeleport Module&r. Hold the module while standing in water and Sneak + Right-click to bind an anchor there, then fire it from the pilot's seat to jump the hull and its crew to that anchor, across dimensions too.",
    "",
    "A jump costs 200,000 power and is refused if the cell holds less, if nothing is bound, or if the anchor is dry or too cramped for the hull. If the anchor gets blocked during the 2.5 second charge, the jump is cancelled and the power comes back.",
  ],
  "quest.2448724FFFA1E08D.title": "&bBubble Anchor",
  "quest.38D9F4CF31A86E71.title": "&cImpulse Laser",
  "quest.0DC9E401CA949038.title": "&2Up to Speed",
  "quest.4A981D058CC1752B.title": "&aParts on Demand",
  "quest.327AC224CD74178C.quest_desc": [
    "Lucky zones and the Prismatic Fishing Rod are separate systems, and they stack.",
    "",
    "Inside a zone with the rod you get the zone's roll and the rod's roll on every catch. Win the catch bar and a bonus treasure roll comes too, and about one bite in seven is a treasure bite that gives two treasure rolls.",
    "",
    "The rarest finds depend on the water. &bAbyssal Trench&r zones can give Abyssal Organs and Budding Prismarine, and &bPrismarine Reef&r zones Prismarine Crystal Shards and Hearts of the Sea.",
  ],
  "task.75DED41F603EA3A2.title": "Smaragdophiles",
  "quest.6CC5E95BCA30A555.quest_desc": [
    "Setting every face of a row of machines one at a time gets old quickly.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aConfiguration Card&r. Sneak + Right-click a machine to copy its settings onto the card, then right-click another block to paste them. Side configuration pastes onto any Nautec machine that has it, so one card sets up a whole row the same way.",
    "",
    "A block's own settings, such as a Confined Spawner's filter or a Resonance Pylon's network, only paste onto the same kind of block. Sneak + Right-click the air to clear the card.",
  ],
  "quest.65E1AE8CEB6387FD.quest_desc": [
    "The deepest materials also make the most expensive weapon in the mod to run.",
    "",
    "Craft an &aAtlantean Rifle&r and hold right-click to fire a continuous beam at whatever you aim at, up to 128 blocks away. Its damage and its power drain both climb over ten seconds of steady fire and reset when you let go.",
    "",
    "It holds 1,000,000 AP and comes out of the crafting table empty, so charge it on a Charger with a strong beam or feed it from a Prismatic Battery. Infinity halves its drain.",
  ],
  "quest.6A774B62B05E366B.quest_desc": [
    "Picking a hull up to charge it is slow going.",
    "",
    "Build a &aSea Scout Dock&r, give it a beam of at least 20 AP and park the hull over it. It charges the hull at 40 power per tick on a 20 AP beam, about 21 minutes from empty to full, and a stronger beam charges faster, twice as fast on four times the power.",
    "",
    "It also clamps an empty hull in place and keeps anyone aboard breathing on the dock's power, even with the hull's own cell empty.",
  ],
  "quest.40653ACDABFB5BE1.quest_desc": [
    "A beam stronger than a machine needs is never wasted.",
    "",
    "Every AP figure in &eNautec&r is the least a machine needs to run. Give it more and most machines run faster. The speed is the square root of the beam divided by what the machine needs. Four times the power runs it twice as fast, nine times runs it three times as fast, and there is no upper limit.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "- &aMixer&r and &2Mutator&r: faster recipes and mutation attempts.",
    "- &aIncubator&r and both &2Bacterial Analyzers&r: faster growth cycles and analysis.",
    "- &aAbyssal Pressure Forge&r: faster forging.",
    "- &aColony Replicator&r and &2Grafting Station&r: faster copying and grafting.",
    "- &aAugmentation Station&r: a faster install, at the pace of the weakest extension in use.",
    "- &aSea Scout Dock&r: faster charging.",
    "- &aBio Reactor&r and &2Industrial Bio Reactor&r: faster production, multiplied with Reactor Speed Upgrades.",
    "- &aDeep Sea Drain&r: more Salt Water every second.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Purity never adds speed. A machine with a purity minimum still stops below it, however much power arrives.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Jade shows each machine's speed and the beam it is getting. Merge sources in a &2Laser Junction&r to build a stronger beam.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Stronger Beams\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:getting_started/stronger_beams.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.6B127FD56FB8487B.title": "&dNeptune's Trident",
  "quest.63A943F3BF9B9561.title": "&bItem Transformation",
  "quest.12FC9636258A86B5.quest_desc": [
    "Clear teal water with glowing spores drifting through it, bright enough to see well over a hundred blocks.",
    "",
    "Shear the three plants of the &bBioluminescent Grove&r, starting with the &aLuminescent Algae&r that lights its floor.",
    "",
    "Lantern Jellies drift through it, and Budding Prismarine forms rarely in the rock 4 to 16 blocks under the floor. Deep Kelp here grows up to 40 blocks tall.",
  ],
  "task.31A9405B5EA7B882.title": "The Deep Oceans",
  "quest.6C763F4FE19B7F3D.quest_desc": [
    "Dropping compound into a beam works, but every batch is a pile of items lying on the floor.",
    "",
    "Build a &aLaser Crafting Matrix&r and point a beam down into its top. It runs every &bItem Transformation&r inside the machine, one craft at a time, so hoppers and pipes can feed it and empty it.",
    "",
    "Every transformation in it asks for a beam of at least its AP and its purity. The panel shows both, green once the beam meets them, and Jade says what the matrix is waiting for. Beams into the sides or bottom do nothing, only the top takes a laser.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: it takes an &2Aquatic Chip&r, from the Mixer or a repaired Damaged Aquatic Chip, and a Laser Channeling Coil, so it comes after both.",
  ],
  "quest.7E24BA960EFA7931.title": "&aThe Mixer",
  "quest.217D267D6A62F48D.quest_desc": [
    "Even with a synthesizer, the Forge still has to sit deep underground.",
    "",
    "Mix an &aAtlantean Pressure Synthesizer&r from a Pressure Synthesizer, a Heart of the Sea, a Nether Star and 4 Ender Pearls with 8,000 mB of Salt Water. With it fitted, the Forge runs at any height with no water above it, and recipes ignore their maximum Y.",
    "",
    "Fitting it swaps out the old synthesizer and hands it back.",
  ],
  "quest.691F8412128B2F33.quest_desc": [
    "Kelp holds oil, if the right strain gets at it.",
    "",
    "Mutate &bHalotrophs&r into &bLipophiles&r with &2Kelp Slurry&r as the catalyst, then run the colony in a Bio Reactor to make &aAlgal Lipid&r. The lipid becomes oil for the Combustion Dynamo.",
    "",
    "The &2Mixer&r makes Kelp Slurry from Kelp and Salt Water. The mutation has a 10% base chance per attempt, and Lipophiles eat Kelp Slurry in the Incubator and in a reactor's nutrient slots.",
  ],
  "quest.2C61275C9E6B6CF8.title": "&bAquarine Copper",
  "quest.10D8036AAEA3BB29.title": "&aTapping the Vents",
  "quest.5D8D7695A3B44155.title": "&5Abyssal Pressure Forge",
  "quest.2FB6F345301719AB.title": "&2Choosing a Mix",
  "quest.6A774B62B05E366B.title": "&3Sea Scout Dock",
  "quest.6C763F4FE19B7F3D.title": "&bHands-Off Transformation",
  "quest.1BF0D5CBD80A80FC.title": "&2Feeding Time",
  "quest.07ACFFA6F8A00E9C.quest_desc": [
    "&eNautec&r can grow your resources for you. Bacteria colonies, fed and powered, produce a steady supply of items or a beam of their own.",
    "",
    "Make a few &aPetri Dishes&r. Each holds one colony, and a colony in a dish neither grows nor ages while it waits.",
    "",
    "The loop goes like this. Graft a colony, analyze it, grow it in an Incubator, mutate it toward the strain you want, then put it to work in a Bio Reactor or burn it in a Bacterial Fuel Cell. At the end of the line, an Industrial Bio Reactor runs nine colonies at once.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"The \", {\"text\": \"Aquatic Biology\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:aquatic_biology/bacteria_introduction.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" pages in the Nautec Guide go deeper on every step.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.2AC4B42D14073C81.quest_desc": [
    "A finished crystal stands on the cradle as a &aCultivated Prismarine Crystal&r.",
    "",
    "Unlike a wild one, it can move. Sneak + Right-click it with a wrench to pick it up, and place it anywhere with six blocks of free space.",
    "",
    "It is also the heart of the Fusion Plant.",
  ],
  "quest.0F1BF451F6A84E98.quest_subtitle": "Unlocks modules and the dock",
  "quest.5F23221A22811049.title": "&3Modules",
  "quest.6B127FD56FB8487B.quest_desc": [
    "Resonant Shards, a Flawless Crystal and Deep Steel Plating make a trident that never breaks.",
    "",
    "Craft &aNeptune's Trident&r. It always flies back to you, and the first thing a thrown one hits releases a tidal shockwave that hurts everything within 5 blocks except you, your pets and your team.",
    "",
    "Sharpness raises the shockwave's damage, and it takes both trident and sword enchantments. Use books on an anvil, since an enchanting table does very little for it.",
  ],
  "task.55979BB0026822CB.title": "Fit a mob organ",
  "quest.3D2B05F88D95FA3C.quest_desc": [
    "Crystal Geodes leave nothing on the ocean floor to show where they are.",
    "",
    "Craft an &aEye of the Sea&r and throw it. Like an Eye of Ender it flies toward the nearest &6Crystal Geode&r, but it is never used up, so throw it as often as you need. When it circles or drops, the geode is under you.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Sneak and right-click to switch what it seeks: &6Crystal Geodes&r, NauTec ruins, Gateways, ocean ruins or ocean monuments.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: each throw that finds something makes &3lucky fishing zones&r form near you twice as often for 5 minutes.",
  ],
  "quest.3C8951D418D9B9DE.title": "&3Hull and Repair",
  "quest.57A356FE9F206C33.title": "&6Hydrothermal Vents",
  "quest.4144063FFB1CD735.quest_desc": [
    "Salt Water is the base of every Mixer recipe, and a bucket dipped in the ocean only brings up plain water here.",
    "",
    "Build a &aDeep Sea Drain&r, a flat multiblock that pumps Salt Water out of the ocean floor into its own tank.",
    "",
    "It only works in an ocean biome with water directly above it, so build it on the sea floor.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Lay a flat 3 by 3 with the &aDeep Sea Drain&r in the middle and eight &2Deep Sea Drain Walls&r around it. All nine blocks directly above it must be water. Right-click the middle block with an Aquarine Steel Wrench to form it.",
    "",
    "It needs more than 20 AP per tick, so merge two catalysts in a &2Laser Junction&r or use a stronger source. With the wrench, right-click one of the four middle wall pieces on any face to make it the laser port. The port always faces outward, so aim the beam into that wall's outer side.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Sneak + Right-click the drain with an empty hand to open it, which only works while it is powered. Open and powered, it pumps 500 mB every second into a 128,000 mB tank on a beam just over 20 AP, and more on a stronger one, twice as much on four times the beam. Take it out with a pipe under the middle block or with a bucket.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: an open drain pulls everything above it down and drowns it, dropped items included. Close it before you swim over it.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Deep Sea Drain\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:laser_chemistry/drain.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.3DD6FFA5C8120682.quest_desc": [
    "Catalysts and a Fuel Cell can run one Bio Reactor, but a real farm wants thousands of AP.",
    "",
    "Make an &aEnergy Converter&r and push FE into it from any generator. Every 10 FE becomes 1 AP, and it sends up to 150 AP per tick out of every side with a receiver in line, split evenly between them.",
    "",
    "Right-click it to set its transmission rate. Match the rate to what your generators supply, and the beam stays steady instead of cutting out when its 4,000,000 FE buffer runs dry.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the converter's beam has a purity of 0. A reactor only counts the AP arriving, so that is fine here, but a recipe that needs purity wants the beam merged with a pure one first.",
  ],
  "quest.269CCC2DAFB7A9B2.title": "&2Ferrophiles",
  "quest.684644505C6D47D4.quest_subtitle": "Unlocks the deep gear",
  "quest.6DBCA290A9EAB706.title": "&bPicking Up Speed",
  "quest.2EBE22F7172BE14E.quest_desc": [
    "Each colony has its own output slot, and emptying three of them by hand gets old quickly.",
    "",
    "Put a Hopper under any block of the reactor's bottom layer. It pulls finished items out of all three output slots, and a pipe on top of the Bio Reactor block does the same.",
    "",
    "When a colony's slot fills up, that colony pauses. It stops aging too, so a full slot only costs you time.",
  ],
  "quest.6F33FC5D591FE07E.quest_desc": [
    "The Sea Scout does not have to stay in the water.",
    "",
    "Fit a &aFlight Module&r. Out of the water the hull holds itself up and flies the way it swims, and it moves half again as fast as it does under water.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"The nose follows your view, \", {\"keybind\": \"key.jump\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: Space\"}}, \" climbs and \", {\"keybind\": \"key.nautec.submarine_descend\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: C\"}}, \" dives, the same as under water. Press \", {\"keybind\": \"key.jump\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: Space\"}}, \" on land to lift off.\"]",
    "",
    "Flying costs 4 power per tick on top of the usual running costs, and the hull falls if the cell runs dry in the air. With nobody at the controls it sinks gently to the ground.",
  ],
  "task.2A38B24EADD0D7FC.title": "Aurrophiles",
  "quest.60D72BA4EEBEF0EF.title": "&2Mutator",
  "quest.732885E121BD83A4.title": "&5Spawner in a Box",
  "quest.101942B6906F4BA0.quest_desc": [
    "With a heart to build around, you can start fitting your body for the sea.",
    "",
    "Build the &aAugmentation Station&r, the multiblock that installs augments into your nine body slots. Augments are permanent, need no power once fitted, and stay with you when you die.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: installing into a filled slot destroys the augment already there.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It is one flat 5 by 5 layer with the corners empty. The station goes in the middle with Polished Prismarine directly north, south, east and west of it, &2Aquarine Steel Blocks&r on the four diagonals, and an Augmentation Station Extension two blocks out on each side.",
    "",
    "Right-click the station with the wrench to form it. All four extensions must be in place, even if you only load one.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Put a &2Claw Robot Arm&r in an extension's top slot and the part in its bottom slot, then fire a beam of at least 25 AP up into that extension from below. Most parts use one extension, while a Vent Carapace takes a Chitin Plate in each of the four, each with its own arm and beam.",
    "",
    "Stand on the middle block, pick a slot and press Apply. The install takes four seconds, and stepping off or losing the beam cancels it with nothing used.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Augmentation Station\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:laser_augmentation/augmentation_station.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.3C08268FC890E1A6.quest_desc": [
    "A &aReactor Fusion Upgrade&r counts as a Speed, a Yield and an Efficiency upgrade in a single slot, and several of them stack.",
    "",
    "It multiplies the reactor's power draw by 4, against about 3.5 for the three separate upgrades. Four of them in an Industrial Bio Reactor triple its speed and make 5 items per cycle on 32% of the nutrients.",
  ],
  "quest.604986E04D0A51CD.title": "&dThe Prismatic Fishing Rod",
  "quest.589A5835042DC2C1.title": "&bBeam Optics",
  "quest.10D8036AAEA3BB29.quest_desc": [
    "Hydrothermal vents stay hot all the time, and that heat can do work.",
    "",
    "Build a &aThermal Vent Tap&r over a 3x3 bed of &2Magma Blocks&r or lava. It boils Salt Water into FE: 350 FE/t with one hot block under it, up to 1,250 FE/t with all nine.",
    "",
    "It uses 10 mB of Salt Water a tick, so pipe it straight from a Deep Sea Drain. Every 1,000 mB it boils leaves a Salt behind, which you can pull out of any side.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: in a Hydrothermal Vents biome it counts three extra hot blocks, as long as at least one is really there.",
  ],
  "quest.65C5C6A7BE9AC4E6.title": "&aFishing Station",
  "quest.5080678667FF621A.quest_desc": [
    "A fed colony never ages, so topping up the nutrient slots is the last job a Bio Reactor still needs you for.",
    "",
    "Feed them automatically. A Hopper on top of the Bio Reactor block, or a pipe into the underside of the base, puts nutrients straight into the nutrient slots, and a full chest of Iron Ore above that hopper keeps three Ferrophiles colonies fed for over nine hours.",
    "",
    "Each nutrient slot holds one kind of item, so a Bio Reactor feeds at most two different nutrients at a time. Fill it with strains that share a nutrient, or with no more strains than it has slots.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the four &bsurface strains&r have no nutrient and always age while they work.",
  ],
  "quest.3EAD190846D5F280.title": "&2Moving the Harvest",
  "quest.4EAA319397136532.quest_desc": [
    "A lot of what you find down there is corroded, Rusty Crates included.",
    "",
    "Craft a bucket of &aEtching Acid&r, pour it into a pit and drop rusty things into it. After a few seconds a Rusty Crate comes out as a plain Crate, a Rusty Gear as a &2Gear&r and an Ancient Valve as a Valve.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The whole dropped stack converts at once, and one etching in three uses up the acid under it, so keep a spare bucket. Gears and Valves go into the Mixer, the Deep Sea Drain and several tools.",
    "",
    "Once the Mixer is running it makes Etching Acid from Salt Water, and the Abyssal Pressure Forge burns it too.",
  ],
  "quest.3EE21DDC41B24798.quest_desc": [
    "The creatures of the Nautec oceans give three more augments:",
    "",
    "- &aAbyssal Eyes&r: from an Abyssal Organ, Eyes slot. Night vision at or below Y 45.",
    "",
    "- &2Photophore Skin&r: from a Luminous Membrane, Body slot. While you are in water, every living thing within 12 blocks glows through walls.",
    "",
    "- &aVent Carapace&r: from four Chitin Plates, Head or Body slot. Adds 4 armor and half knockback resistance, and fire burns you for half as long.",
    "",
    "Flight, the Dolphin Fin and Photophore Skin all want the Body slot, so the Carapace is best fitted in the Head slot.",
  ],
  "quest.2E063BB63F0D37CC.title": "&5The Abyssal Maw",
  "quest.3110B6A87C933A2D.quest_desc": [
    "Grafting by hand needs the right biome and a lucky click.",
    "",
    "Build a &aGrafting Station&r. Give it an empty Petri Dish, one of the blocks &eJEI&r lists under Bacteria Grafting, and 4,000 mB of Salt Water, and every minute it puts a fresh colony in the dish. No biome is needed and no try is wasted.",
    "",
    "It needs a beam of at least 100 AP at purity 2.8, into any face except the front. A Prismarine Crystal beam fed straight in works, but one bounced off a Prismatic Mirror drops to 2.7 and is too weak.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Budding Prismarine gives Lithophiles directly, which skips the long mutation from Thermophiles.",
  ],
  "quest.16B9BE43A2E632A0.quest_desc": [
    "Every Prismarine Crystal so far has been one you found in a geode. Now you can grow one.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aDormant Crystal Seed&r. It does nothing on its own yet, because it has to be awakened first.",
  ],
  "quest.51EC17DA8C101A1E.title": "&2Aurrophiles",
  "quest.79556AE1437DA3EC.title": "&2Lithophiles",
  "quest.39723418051CB84F.quest_desc": [
    "Running a pipe to every machine gets messy once a base spreads out.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aNautechnical Distributor&r and put chests or tanks against its sides. Sneak + Right-click it with an empty hand to start linking, do the same on each machine on the face it should use, then finish on the Distributor again.",
    "",
    "It links up to 64 blocks within 256 blocks. Every 4 ticks it collects their outputs into its neighbors and keeps their inputs stocked. To set an input, Sneak-click an item onto an empty input slot of a Nautec machine, or select any linked block in the Distributor's screen and add requests there.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: on other mods' machines the linked face decides what it collects, so link a furnace by its bottom. It moves items and fluids, not power.",
  ],
  "quest.6A82B052670383C2.title": "&5Across the Void",
  "quest.5D8D7695A3B44155.quest_desc": [
    "Unlike the other machines, the Forge only runs deep under the sea with water piled on top of it.",
    "",
    "Build an &aAbyssal Pressure Forge&r at Y 0 or lower with the eight blocks directly above it all water source blocks. Give it a beam of at least 40 AP into a side or its top, and fill its tank with &2Etching Acid&r.",
    "",
    "Each press uses 250 mB of acid, and if any condition fails partway through, the press starts again from zero. A dry shaft does not count, however deep it goes.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: a Bacterial Fuel Cell at full purity covers both recipes, and so does a crystal's beam turned once by a Prismatic Mirror.",
  ],
  "task.14D161928088EB9D.title": "Metallophiles",
  "quest.39B9122F5229D65D.quest_desc": [
    "One converter tops out at 150 AP per tick, and an Industrial Bio Reactor drains that fast.",
    "",
    "Put an &aEnergy Conversion Upgrade&r in the converter's first upgrade slot. Each one adds 150 AP/t, and the slot holds eight.",
    "",
    "The &2Advanced and Ultimate&r upgrades go in the second and third slots and add 500 and 1,500 AP/t each. With every slot full a converter sends 17,350 AP/t and burns 173,500 FE/t, so build the generators before the upgrades.",
  ],
  "quest.2CDD35D21A370805.title": "&bRouting a Beam",
  "quest.615324CE00859A3E.title": "&aPrismarine Reef",
  "quest.269CCC2DAFB7A9B2.quest_subtitle": "Your first bacterial metal",
  "quest.06CC49037F4B3008.title": "&2Bio Reactor",
  "quest.0027241295FBA78B.quest_desc": [
    "Twelve augment parts are crafted rather than hunted, and most of them are limbs.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aHydro Drill Arm&r to start. It removes the slowdown for mining with your head under water, as long as you stand on the bottom.",
    "",
    "The other arms pull in dropped items or throw tridents and potions on a key, and the legs give you a leap, step up, no fall damage or faster walking. Two copies of the same leg do nothing more than one, so fit two different ones.",
  ],
  "quest.54EABC84BD158EC6.title": "&5Charged on the Go",
  "task.1B102379E3BDADE3.title": "Feed a colony",
  "quest.77FFEC3A2289F5C2.title": "&bWelcome to Nautec",
  "task.3CB14C0D14EF28BD.title": "Read",
  "task.57E908F40C219B1A.title": "Adamantophiles",
  "quest.6F403759246877FB.title": "&2Smaragdophiles",
  "quest.4C10A4FE30CFFDDA.quest_desc": [
    "With nothing in its filter slot, a tap lets everything through.",
    "",
    "Put a &aFilter&r in the tap to open 9 item and 9 fluid filter slots on every face, with separate lists for Input and Output. Each list can be a whitelist or a blacklist.",
    "",
    "Click a slot with an item to set it, or drag items and fluids straight in from &eJEI&r. Shift-click a set slot to choose whether it matches components exactly. An &2Intricate Filter&r opens all 27 item slots.",
  ],
  "quest.718C50DBF9A20D01.quest_desc": [
    "A Bio Reactor tops out at three colonies, two nutrient slots and two upgrades.",
    "",
    "Build an &aIndustrial Bio Reactor&r, the multiblock for mass production. It runs nine colonies with an output slot each, three nutrient slots and four upgrade slots, and every colony works at the same speed, eats the same nutrients and takes the same upgrades as in the Bio Reactor.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"The controller is crafted around a \", {\"text\": \"Bio Reactor\", \"color\": \"dark_green\"}, \" with Deep Steel Plating and Resonant Shards, so it comes after \", {\"text\": \"Pressing the Deep\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"684644505C6D47D4\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to Pressing the Deep Quest\"}}, \".\"]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The frame is 5 by 5 and 4 tall, built in layers around a 3 by 3 by 2 culture chamber that must be empty air, with no water and no blocks in it:",
    "",
    "- &bBottom layer&r: Dark Prismarine Pillars in the corners, Polished Prismarine everywhere else.",
    "",
    "- &bLayers 2 and 3&r: Dark Prismarine Pillars in the corners and &2Bacteria Containment Shields&r along the edges, with the middle left empty.",
    "",
    "- &bRoof&r: Dark Prismarine Pillars in the corners, &2Aquarine Steel Blocks&r everywhere else.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The &aIndustrial Bio Reactor&r takes the place of the middle shield of the north wall in layer 2, and the structure only forms facing that way.",
    "",
    "The full build is 82 blocks with the controller, and no other size or block works. That is a pillar in each of the 16 corners, 23 shields, and 21 each of Polished Prismarine and Aquarine Steel Blocks.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Industrial Bio Reactor\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:aquatic_biology/industrial_bio_reactor.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide for a 3D view of the build.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.39B9122F5229D65D.title": "&2Turning It Up",
  "quest.3ABC3462415EC6A6.quest_desc": [
    "Stone rings stand on small prismarine platforms on the ocean floor, each with a Gateway block at its base.",
    "",
    "Find a wild &aGateway&r ring and look at it. It opens by itself when you or your &2Sea Scout&r come within about 12 blocks, and it needs no power.",
    "",
    "Each wild ring is half of a pair with its own address. The first trip through it builds the other half in another ocean, 1,250 to 1,750 blocks away, and sends you there. From then on the two rings are a fixed route both ways.",
  ],
  "quest.062E3FE8A6A3A450.quest_desc": [
    "Algal Lipid is one Mixer recipe away from oil, and oil burns.",
    "",
    "Build a &aCombustion Dynamo&r and pipe in oil and water. It makes 320 FE/t and pushes it into anything touching it, burning 1 mB of oil every 10 ticks and 1 mB of water every tick.",
    "",
    "The &2Mixer&r turns 1 Algal Lipid and 250 mB of Salt Water into 1,000 mB of oil. All oil in this pack is Oritech's, so the dynamo burns oil from Oritech's own machines and oil lakes as well.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each fluid has its own tank and only goes into that one, so a single pipe can carry both.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: &2Redstone&r in the additive slot raises output to 480 FE/t for a minute of burning, at 10% more oil and water. The minute only counts down while it burns.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Combustion Dynamo\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:getting_started/combustion_dynamo.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.3CEA250892D82970.quest_desc": [
    "&eNautec&r adds four ocean biomes alongside the vanilla ones. They only generate in new chunks, so in an older world they sit past the edge of the ground you have explored.",
    "",
    "All four count as oceans, so lucky fishing zones, the Deep Sea Drain, Nautec structures and shipwrecks all work in them. Each has its own plants, creatures and fishing loot.",
    "",
    "Collect every Nautec plant with Shears, since any other tool breaks it for nothing.",
  ],
  "quest.2EAF6EB6688A64EB.title": "&2Redstone and Lapis",
  "quest.3C58133AB9909BC3.quest_desc": [
    "Some colonies are worth more as power than as items.",
    "",
    "Build a &aBacterial Fuel Cell&r and right-click it with a dish to load the colony. It burns the colony into a beam that leaves from the side opposite the face you looked at when placing it, and only while a receiver sits on that side.",
    "",
    "Power is 24 AP per point of Production Rate, and the colony burns faster at the same pace, so a fast colony gives the same energy sooner. Purity rises with Mutation Resistance, up to 2.5 at the cap.",
    "",
    "It never ages a colony and burns any strain, including the surface strains that make nothing in a reactor.",
  ],
  "quest.1D7AAD2487528786.quest_desc": [
    "This is what the chamber is for.",
    "",
    "Load Prismarine Crystal Shards into the chamber and let it run. Every critical turns one shard into a &aResonant Shard&r, so a full stack works through on its own.",
    "",
    "Resonant Shards go into Gateways, the Abyssal Pressure Forge and Neptune's Trident, and the Forge presses them into Flawless Prismarine Crystals. Hoppers can feed shards in from the sides or the top.",
  ],
  "quest.5EB9CF37E089845E.title": "&bChanneling Coils",
  "task.0E7080F8C4AD0861.title": "Pick an upgrade set",
  "quest.5080678667FF621A.title": "&2A Steady Diet",
  "quest.2EBE22F7172BE14E.title": "&2Automated Harvest",
  "quest.0E2C04911CA2D653.title": "&5Resonance Chamber",
  "quest.5EB9CF37E089845E.quest_desc": [
    "With a pure beam to work with, the &2Burnt Coils&r you have been pulling out of crates and guardians are finally useful.",
    "",
    "Hold a Burnt Coil in a beam of purity 1.5 or more for 10 seconds to repair it into a &aLaser Channeling Coil&r. The Charger, the Prismatic Battery, the biology machines and most later builds all need them.",
    "",
    "This early, the crystal's beam is the only way to reach that purity. The Focusing Lens and the Bacterial Fuel Cell both need coils of their own.",
  ],
  "quest.6351729D4F3ED437.quest_desc": [
    "Vanilla ocean mobs drop organs that fit straight into the station with no crafting:",
    "",
    "- &aGuardian Eye&r: Eyes slot. Fires a guardian beam at what you look at while you hold its key.",
    "",
    "- &2Dolphin Fin&r: Body slot. Dolphin's Grace II whenever your head is under water.",
    "",
    "- &aDrowned Lungs&r: Lungs slot. Your air never runs out under water.",
    "",
    "- &2Eldritch Heart&r: Heart slot. Heals half a heart every second in water.",
    "",
    "Guardians drop eyes about one kill in forty, Dolphins drop fins about one in five, and Drowned drop lungs about one in twenty.",
  ],
  "quest.675D7B6F6826316D.quest_desc": [
    "With the drain running, you have a steady supply of Salt Water.",
    "",
    "Fill a &aSalt Water Bucket&r from the drain, or connect a pipe under its middle block. The Mixer draws 1,000 mB of it for every batch.",
    "",
    "Away from the sea, craft a &2Water Bucket&r with Salt to get a Salt Water Bucket. Salt turns up as a catch in lucky fishing zones.",
    "",
    "[\"\", { \"text\": \"Productive Bees\", \"color\": \"green\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"586E18023A595A6C\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"value\": {\"translate\":\"Go To Productive Bees Quests\"},\"action\":\"show_text\"} }, \" can also automate salt water!\" ]",
  ],
  "quest.30A058E82CF6766A.title": "&bWave Jet",
  "quest.480870A483F8E2C9.title": "&bLong Distance Laser",
  "quest.0E2C04911CA2D653.quest_desc": [
    "The next materials need a purity that no catalyst, fuel cell or lens can reach.",
    "",
    "Build a &aResonance Chamber&r and feed it a purity 3.0 beam of at least 20 AP into a side or its top. It stores the beam as charge, and each time the charge reaches critical it crafts one item and starts again.",
    "",
    "Only a Prismarine Crystal gives 3.0. Put the chamber right under the crystal's bottom tip, or catch that beam in a &2Laser Junction&r and send it sideways, since a junction keeps the purity where a mirror costs a tenth of it.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: a chamber that reaches critical with nothing to craft vents and hurts everything within four blocks. Load it before the beam and keep the output clear, which a hopper underneath does for you.",
  ],
  "quest.747774F0F1C5F3E3.quest_desc": [
    "Four strains can be grafted without going near the deep ocean, each from a common block in the right biome:",
    "",
    "- &bThermophiles&r: Netherrack in the Nether.",
    "",
    "- &bMethanogens&r: Podzol in a forest.",
    "",
    "- &bHalobacteria&r: Sand on a beach.",
    "",
    "- &bCyanobacteria&r: Stone in an ocean.",
    "",
    "Each try has a 40% chance. None of the four makes anything or can be fed in an Incubator, so they exist to be mutated, and Thermophiles is where the metal chain begins.",
  ],
  "quest.691F8412128B2F33.title": "&2Lipophiles",
  "quest.47C148C5CD8432DE.title": "&2Incubator",
  "quest.63A943F3BF9B9561.quest_desc": [
    "An item lying anywhere inside a powered beam, between the block that sends it and the block that receives it, is checked against the &bItem Transformation&r recipes.",
    "",
    "The whole dropped stack changes at once, and every item in it gives the recipe's full output. When more than one recipe matches, the beam uses the one with the highest purity it can meet.",
    "",
    "The item has to stay in the beam for the full recipe time. If it is pushed out or the beam drops for a moment, it starts over. The purity that counts is set by the block that sends the beam, and &eJEI&r lists every transformation with the purity it asks for.",
  ],
  "quest.6F33FC5D591FE07E.title": "&3Flight Module",
  "quest.4AEFD35B32DD2489.title": "&dThe Prismarine Crystal",
  "quest.0131C83A87A25AF4.quest_desc": [
    "A fresh colony shows its strain and nothing else, with question marks where the numbers should be.",
    "",
    "Build a &aBacterial Analyzer&r, two blocks tall, and fire a beam of at least 5 AP up into its bottom face. Put a fresh dish in the left slot and it comes back readable after three seconds.",
    "",
    "Hold Shift over an analyzed dish to see its product and four stats:",
    "",
    "- &bGrowth Rate&r: multiplies what each Incubator cycle adds.",
    "",
    "- &bProduction Rate&r: how fast the Bio Reactor makes items, and a Fuel Cell's power.",
    "",
    "- &bMutation Resistance&r: lowers Mutator success and softens failures, and sets a Fuel Cell's purity.",
    "",
    "- &bLifespan&r: how many ticks it can work unfed in a reactor before it turns Senescent.",
  ],
  "quest.3CEA250892D82970.title": "&3The Deep Oceans",
  "quest.6C9E2A1AD6F50E3F.title": "&2Grafting",
  "quest.2112D4B209CCCE84.quest_desc": [
    "This is the whole bacteria line working together, from capped colonies and nutrient chests to upgrades, converters and pipes.",
    "",
    "Deliver 50,000 &aIron Ingots&r. One Industrial Bio Reactor of capped Ferrophiles with two Speed and two Yield Upgrades makes about 4,355 a minute on 4,562 AP, so a running line fills this in about 12 minutes.",
    "",
    "A reactor's output is capped by its slots and upgrades, so grow by building more of the same unit, each with its own nutrient chest, pipes and converters. Three of them make over 10,000 iron a minute.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the task takes the ingots, so pipe the line into a &2Task Screen&r from &eFTB Quests&r rather than emptying your storage.",
  ],
  "quest.1BF0D5CBD80A80FC.quest_desc": [
    "A colony ages while it works, one tick of its &bLifespan&r for every tick of progress, unless the reactor keeps it fed.",
    "",
    "Put the colony's nutrient in one of the Bio Reactor's two nutrient slots. The colony fills a nutrient buffer from it, the thin bar beside the colony, and works without aging for as long as the buffer lasts.",
    "",
    "One item adds 1,200 ticks, a minute of work, so each working colony eats about one nutrient a minute. It is the same item the strain eats in the Incubator, and &eJEI&r's Colony Feeding category lists every one.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: a starving colony past its Lifespan is &cSenescent&r and loses 2% of its size every second it works. One nutrient stops the loss at once, but only an Incubator cycle makes the colony young again.",
  ],
  "quest.48C6A0778FE5BC1E.title": "&dPowering a Gateway",
  "quest.3BA1F3D850C3C624.quest_desc": [
    "Laser power can travel a long way, but a satellite takes it anywhere under open sky.",
    "",
    "Build an &aUplink Array&r and a &2Downlink Array&r, and join both to one network the same way you set up a pylon. Then right-click the uplink with a &aPrism Satellite&r to launch it. Both arrays need open sky above them. Only solid blocks get in the way, so water, glass and leaves are fine.",
    "",
    "Fire beams into the uplink, or pipe FE into it. Every downlink on the network fires the AP into the laser blocks around it and pushes the FE into anything touching it, after a 10% loss. Downlinks with a higher priority fill first, and each has its own limit, both set at the top of its screen.",
    "",
    "The grid is not tied to one dimension. A downlink in a dimension with no uplink of its own still gets power, with 5% less purity.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Prism Satellite\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:deep_engineering/prism_satellite.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.53F8764099C14F93.quest_desc": [
    "Everything you have learned about beams leads here.",
    "",
    "Set a &aFusion Controller&r into a side wall, facing out, with the crystal 2 to 5 blocks straight behind it. That distance sets the chamber size. The controller checks the build every 2 seconds and tells you the first thing that is wrong.",
    "",
    "Pipe Salt Water into the controller or a Fusion Port, then fire beams of purity 2.0 or more into the backs of the injectors. A cold plant takes 5,000,000 AP to ignite before it makes any power.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Each AP of beam makes up to 50 FE, scaled by purity up to 3.0, and each mB of Salt Water covers 2,000 FE. The chamber width caps the output:",
    "- 3 wide: 20,000 FE/t",
    "- 5 wide: 50,000 FE/t",
    "- 7 wide: 100,000 FE/t",
    "- 9 wide: 200,000 FE/t",
    "",
    "Each Containment Coil raises that cap by 4,000 FE/t, up to 300,000 FE/t. The controller and every port push FE into whatever touches them from outside.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: without fuel or a beam the plasma cools completely in 20 seconds, and the next start costs the full 5,000,000 AP again.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Fusion Plant\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:deep_engineering/fusion_plant.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.5A93784A7A8E2997.quest_desc": [
    "Two modules keep the hull in one piece.",
    "",
    "Fit an &aArmour Module&r for tougher plating and no knockback, and a &2Shield Module&r that pays for hits out of the cell at 10,000 power per heart.",
    "",
    "Fire the Shield Module and it discharges instead, knocking back, hurting and stunning everything within 5 blocks for 3 seconds. That includes players and pets, so check who is nearby first.",
  ],
  "quest.6843F1AA23F6FFB4.title": "&2Copy That",
  "quest.604986E04D0A51CD.quest_desc": [
    "Lucky zones work with any rod. This one adds a bonus roll to every catch, wherever you fish.",
    "",
    "Make a &aPrismatic Fishing Rod&r. When something bites, a catch bar opens for three seconds and names itself:",
    "",
    "- &bSomething is biting&r: strike once while the marker is in the green window.",
    "- &bIt is fighting you&r: three short windows, one strike in each, in order.",
    "- &bIt is running with the line&r: press as the marker enters the green, hold, and let go before it leaves.",
    "",
    "Strike with Space, Enter or left-click, then reel in straight away. Winning adds a bonus treasure roll, and missing never costs you anything compared with a plain rod.",
  ],
  "quest.47C148C5CD8432DE.quest_desc": [
    "A new colony starts small, a few hundred at most, and size is what makes it productive.",
    "",
    "Build an &aIncubator&r and power it with at least 20 AP into its top or bottom. Put the colony in the bacteria slot and its nutrient in the item slot, and every five-second cycle adds size.",
    "",
    "Growth is rolled from the recipe and multiplied by the colony's Growth Rate, and each cycle has a chance to use up the nutrient. Metal strains eat the ore of their own metal, and &eJEI&r's Bacteria Incubation category lists the rest.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the four surface strains have no nutrient, so mutate them first.",
  ],
  "quest.2271043535B4D61D.title": "&5Wireless Machines",
  "task.358B0BE83224C4E8.title": "&eObserve&r: Prismarine Crystal",
  "quest.62D4AD580B20C416.title": "&2Deep Strains",
  "quest.2FD63A10FF3E5F24.quest_desc": [
    "The deepest and darkest of the four, far from land in cold climates, with visibility down to about twenty blocks.",
    "",
    "Dive into an &bAbyssal Trench&r and shear some &aAbyssal Coral&r off the floor.",
    "",
    "Drowned spawn far more often here, and the &cAbyssal Maw&r hunts the dark water below Y 40. The depth also makes it the best place for an Abyssal Pressure Forge later on.",
  ],
  "task.3FD62D295DEAEBFD.title": "Gateway Addresses",
  "quest.1FA84DC387722607.title": "&dBuilding the Chamber",
  "quest.79556AE1437DA3EC.quest_desc": [
    "Every metal strain descends from &bLithophiles&r, a colony that makes Stone.",
    "",
    "Get a Lithophiles colony. Mutate &bThermophiles&r with Stone as the catalyst, or graft one straight from a Budding Prismarine block placed in a Prismarine Reef.",
    "",
    "The mutation has a 5% base chance per attempt, so the graft is much faster if you have a Budding Prismarine block to spare. Lithophiles eat Stone in the Incubator.",
  ],
  "quest.2E063BB63F0D37CC.quest_desc": [
    "The &cAbyssal Maw&r only spawns in dark water below Y 40 in the Trench, and it attacks players on sight from up to 24 blocks away.",
    "",
    "Kill three of them. Each has 24 health and bites for 6, so come armored.",
    "",
    "Each one drops an &aAbyssal Organ&r, the part for the &dAbyssal Eyes&r augment, which gives night vision in the deep.",
  ],
  "quest.24C3B87362113EA7.title": "&2Containment Shields",
  "task.0C0C7408892F902B.title": "Stronger Beams",
  "quest.3F86B2A1DD7D5AD3.quest_desc": [
    "A running beam does more than carry power. Drop an item into it and the beam can turn it into something else.",
    "",
    "Craft some Aquarine Steel Compound and drop it on the ground under a powered beam to make &aAquarine Steel Ingots&r. Any purity works, so one catalyst firing into a relay is enough, and most machines in the mod are built from this metal.",
    "",
    "Under a beam of purity 2.0 or more each compound comes out as two ingots instead of one.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the beam burns anything standing in it, you included, so drop items in from the side.",
  ],
  "quest.732885E121BD83A4.quest_desc": [
    "Spawners make good loot and bad neighbors.",
    "",
    "Use a &aSpawner Confinement Matrix&r on a spawner to turn it into a &2Confined Spawner&r. Nothing spawns anymore. Each cycle it rolls the mob's drops as if a player had killed it and stores them inside, ready to pipe out.",
    "",
    "Power it with a laser beam into any face; it uses 50 AP/t while it runs. Its filter can whitelist or blacklist drops by item or tag, and once it is empty, Sneak + Right-click with an empty hand gets the matrix back.",
    "",
    "It also keeps the experience its mobs would drop as liquid experience, ready to pipe out or collect with a bucket. Breaking it with a pickaxe drops the Confined Spawner itself, mob, settings and stored experience included, so you can move it.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Confined Spawner\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:laser_chemistry/confined_spawner.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.06CC49037F4B3008.quest_desc": [
    "A grown colony is ready to work.",
    "",
    "Build a &aBio Reactor&r, the multiblock that puts up to three colonies to work making items. Each makes its strain's item for as long as the reactor has power, and making items never uses the colony up.",
    "",
    "The bigger the colony and the higher its Production Rate, the faster it works. Deep strains such as Lithophiles or Halotrophs give you a first harvest straight away.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The frame is 3 by 3 by 2. Both layers have Dark Prismarine Pillars in the corners and &2Bacteria Containment Shields&r on the edges, eight of each in all.",
    "",
    "The bottom layer has Polished Prismarine in the middle and the top layer has the Bio Reactor. Right-click it with the wrench to form it, and chat names any block that is wrong.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Turn one of the four top-layer shields into a hatch with the wrench and point a beam down into it. You can open more than one hatch, and their power adds together.",
    "",
    "The reactor needs 25 AP for itself plus 25 per colony, so 100 AP with all three slots full, and below that nothing runs. A catalyst gives 12 at most, so merge beams in a Laser Junction first.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Bio Reactor\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:aquatic_biology/bio_reactor.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.07DB72267839D8D7.title": "&3Speed and Stealth",
  "quest.3DD6FFA5C8120682.title": "&2Converting Power",
  "quest.2D0A433D8257F15E.quest_desc": [
    "Every finished cycle drops one item into the colony's output slot, and that number can go up.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aReactor Yield Upgrade&r and slot it in. Each one adds an item to every completed cycle, so one gives 2 items per cycle, two give 3 and four give 5, and each multiplies the power draw by 1.8.",
    "",
    "For items per AP it beats Speed, giving twice the output for 1.8 times the power where Speed gives 1.5 times the output for 1.6 times. The output slot needs room for the whole batch before a cycle can finish.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"It needs \", {\"text\": \"Flawless Prismarine Crystals\", \"color\": \"dark_green\"}, \" and plating from \", {\"text\": \"Pressing the Deep\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"684644505C6D47D4\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to Pressing the Deep Quest\"}}, \".\"]",
  ],
  "quest.2392DE947119DD60.quest_desc": [
    "The simplest module needs nothing but daylight.",
    "",
    "Fit a &aSolar Module&r. While the sun is up and nothing solid sits between the hull and the sky, it adds about 20 power per tick to the cell, through the water and with nobody aboard.",
    "",
    "It does nothing in dimensions without a day cycle, such as the Nether and the End, and a Sea Scout Dock still fills a hull twice as fast.",
  ],
  "quest.2D0A433D8257F15E.title": "&2Bumper Crop",
  "task.48FA27DCF4C951BE.title": "Plan by Strain Yield",
  "quest.101942B6906F4BA0.title": "&dAugmentation Station",
  "quest.674023982F732B18.quest_desc": [
    "Put the Dormant Crystal Seed in the Resonance Chamber and hold it at purity 3.0 to awaken it into a &aPrismarine Crystal Seed&r.",
    "",
    "That is the same purity you used for Resonant Shards, so the setup you already have works.",
  ],
  "quest.480870A483F8E2C9.quest_desc": [
    "Sixteen blocks is not far when your machines are on the sea floor and your crystal is down in a geode.",
    "",
    "Make a &aLong Distance Laser&r. It works like a relay with a 64 block reach and passes on the same power and purity.",
    "",
    "Its front, where the beam leaves, faces you when you place it, so stand where the beam should go and look back toward the source. The beam passes through water, kelp and seagrass but stops at glass and any other solid block.",
  ],
  "quest.6F403759246877FB.quest_desc": [
    "The last link in the chain.",
    "",
    "Mutate &bAdamantophiles&r with an Emerald to get &bSmaragdophiles&r, which make Emeralds and feed on Emerald Ore. With a Strain Yield of 0.1, they are the slowest strain in the chain.",
    "",
    "From here the only way forward is better stats. Every mutation carries them over with a small shift, so the Growth and Production Rate you bred at each step come along.",
  ],
  "quest.3B7FCE8FEC7A4C26.quest_desc": [
    "A Gateway's address is the color of the four chevrons at its upper left, upper right, lower left and lower right, as seen from the front. Each one is White, Light Blue, Cyan, Blue, Purple, Magenta, Lime or Black.",
    "",
    "Right-click near a chevron with one of those dyes to change it, or right-click the ring with an empty hand to set all four on the address screen. Changing the address is free, and the dye is not used up.",
    "",
    "Travel stays in one dimension and always picks the nearest ring with the same address, so give each pair its own. Give a wild ring the address of one you built and it links there instead of to its far half.",
  ],
  "quest.2C30458D324A4AD9.quest_desc": [
    "Carbophages are one step away from real metal.",
    "",
    "Mutate &bCarbophages&r with a Copper Ingot to get &bMetallophiles&r, which make Copper Ingots.",
    "",
    "Metallophiles sits in the middle of the chain. Redstone and Lapis strains come off it, and it feeds on Copper Ore.",
  ],
  "quest.4A981D058CC1752B.quest_desc": [
    "Machine parts used to come only from &2Rusty Crates&r and luck.",
    "",
    "Every one of them now has a guaranteed recipe. Look up the Gear, Valve, Whisk, Burnt Coil, Aquatic Chip and Atlantic Gold Ingot in JEI when a crate run comes up short.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: most of the new recipes run in the &2Mixer&r with Salt Water, and Gears come four at a time from a Cast Iron Block held in a purity 2.5 beam.",
  ],
  "quest.3ABC3462415EC6A6.title": "&dWild Gateways",
  "quest.33EB7286E6E1DE70.quest_desc": [
    "Deep under the floor of the &bAbyssal Trench&r and the &bBioluminescent Grove&r, rare blocks grow crystal the way budding amethyst does.",
    "",
    "Find a block of &aBudding Prismarine&r 4 to 16 blocks under either floor and mine it with &bSilk Touch&r, or fish one up as lucky zone treasure in the Trench. Place it wherever you want your farm.",
    "",
    "Buds sprout on any face with air or water next to them and grow into a &2Prismarine Cluster&r. A cluster drops two shards, more with Fortune, and a bud broken early drops nothing.",
  ],
  "quest.5A93784A7A8E2997.title": "&3Armour and Shields",
  "quest.66A97821D6355722.title": "&dBuoyancy Tank",
  "quest.54EABC84BD158EC6.quest_desc": [
    "Craft a &aResonance Charm&r and right-click a pylon, an Uplink Array or a Downlink Array to bind it to that network.",
    "",
    "Worn in a charm slot, it charges the FE items in your inventory, armor and curios, plus the Atlantean Rifle and Prismatic Battery, at up to 2,000 FE/t. It draws from the network's Uplink Arrays first and its sending pylons after that.",
    "",
    "Right-click the air with it to see the network it is bound to and set its priority against your downlinks. Sneak + Right-click the air to unbind it.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: it also works as a Prism Monocle, so you can read beams while wearing it.",
  ],
  "quest.38D9F4CF31A86E71.quest_desc": [
    "Sooner or later something down there needs dealing with.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Fit an \", {\"text\": \"Impulse Laser Module\", \"color\": \"green\"}, \", select it, and hold \", {\"keybind\": \"key.attack\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: Left Button\"}}, \" or \", {\"keybind\": \"key.nautec.submarine_ability\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: F\"}}, \" to fire two beams from the nose. They charge for half a second, then grow stronger over the next 5 seconds.\"]",
    "",
    "Each beam hits the first creature in its path, up to 64 blocks away, every quarter second. A hit deals 2 damage rising to 6, plus up to 1.25% of the target's maximum health, and ignores armor. It draws 400 power a tick at first and 1,400 at full strength, and stops when the cell runs dry.",
  ],
  "quest.33EB7286E6E1DE70.title": "&bBudding Prismarine",
  "quest.0027241295FBA78B.title": "&dCrafted Limbs",
  "quest.5085CFD8AB65A4B3.quest_desc": [
    "Lasers are not the only power the sea gives you.",
    "",
    "Build a &aTidal Rotor&r. It is the first Nautec machine that makes FE, and it only needs cast iron, copper and redstone.",
    "",
    "It runs waterlogged in an ocean biome, making 40 FE/t in a shallow spot and up to 80 FE/t when every block around it is water and 24 blocks of water sit above it. Sink it on the sea floor rather than in a pond.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Ocean Generators\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:getting_started/ocean_generators.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "task.1E649949BFF4510A.title": "Other Metals",
  "quest.1485B05D33FAFFE5.quest_desc": [
    "The same crystal beam that repairs coils also makes the best fuel a catalyst can burn.",
    "",
    "Drop Prismarine Crystals into a beam of purity 2.0 or more to make &aPrismarine Crystal Shards&r. Each crystal gives two shards after 8 seconds.",
    "",
    "Shards burn at purity 1.2 in a catalyst and go into the optics, the Prismatic Battery, the Augmentation Station and most advanced builds. Lucky fishing zones turn them up too, and an infused &2Aquarine Steel Pickaxe&r can chip them off a Prismarine Crystal.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: every pickaxe hit has a one in four chance to shatter the crystal for good, so only chip at one you are not using for purity.",
  ],
  "quest.4C10A4FE30CFFDDA.title": "&bSorting the Flow",
  "task.0337ECF4A872B69E.title": "Automate the nutrients",
  "quest.66E132073DA81E4A.quest_desc": [
    "Silt Skippers are small passive fish that school in groups of up to eight in the Trench, the Grove and the Reef.",
    "",
    "Right-click one with a Water Bucket to scoop up a &aBucket of Silt Skipper&r.",
    "",
    "&7&oA bucketed one makes a fine aquarium fish.&r",
  ],
  "quest.46E756E1EDEF8DE0.quest_desc": [
    "The first step down the metal chain turns stone into fuel.",
    "",
    "Mutate &bLithophiles&r with Coal to get &bCarbophages&r, which make Coal in the Bio Reactor.",
    "",
    "Like every link in this chain, the mutation has a 5% base chance and the new strain makes the item that created it. Carbophages eat Coal Ore in the Incubator.",
  ],
  "task.5C9AC0099F683CB0.title": "Carbophages",
  "quest.148338A58609D18D.quest_desc": [
    "A lucky zone roll can hook a creature instead of an item. Reel it in and the animal is released at your bobber.",
    "",
    "Live cod can come up anywhere. The &bBioluminescent Grove&r gives live Silt Skippers and Lantern Jellies, the &bPrismarine Reef&r live tropical fish, and the &bAbyssal Trench&r live squid.",
  ],
  "quest.29CB4422765935BC.quest_desc": [
    "Augments are fitted at the Augmentation Station, and the station is built around a heart.",
    "",
    "Kill an Elder Guardian for an &aEldritch Heart&r. Each one has roughly a three in five chance to drop at least one.",
    "",
    "Keep the first for the station. More go into the Sea Scout and two of its modules, and a heart fitted as an augment heals you while you are in water.",
  ],
  "quest.48C6A0778FE5BC1E.quest_desc": [
    "A wild ring that has never been moved runs on its own. A crafted or moved one needs AP.",
    "",
    "Point a laser at the &aGateway&r block at the bottom of the ring. It stores 5,000 AP and uses 100 AP every tick while it is open, so a beam of 100 AP or more keeps it open for as long as you like.",
    "",
    "A ring opens when a player or a &2Sea Scout&r comes within about 12 blocks and closes a few seconds after everyone leaves. A redstone signal into the Gateway block holds it shut, and a &2Prism Monocle&r shows its address, its stored power and whether it is open.",
  ],
  "task.350F4A092381C79B.title": "Lucky Zones",
  "quest.39723418051CB84F.title": "&bNo Pipes Needed",
  "quest.1F00BCA0042DB923.quest_desc": [
    "The Distributor links machines from a distance. Sometimes you just want a pipe.",
    "",
    "Craft &aCurrent Conduit&r and lay it between the blocks you want to connect. One line carries items, fluids and FE together. Plain conduit never connects to a machine by itself, so nothing moves until the line has a tap.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click a conduit next to your machines with the &2Aquarine Steel Wrench&r to turn it into a &aConduit Tap&r. A tap reaches every block it touches, and doing the same again turns it back into conduit.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Right-click a tap with an empty hand to open it. Pick a face, then on the Setup tab set each resource to Input (the network takes it out of that block), Output (the network puts it in) or both.",
    "",
    "The Input and Output tabs each have their own redstone rule and filter. Input also chooses how a face shares out what it takes: Round Robin, Nearest First or Random. Output has a priority, and higher priority destinations fill first.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: a plain wrench click on a conduit side stops it joining the block next to it, so two lines can run side by side without merging.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Current Conduits\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:deep_engineering/current_conduits.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.5060BFECF1EE9856.title": "&dGateways",
  "quest.615324CE00859A3E.quest_desc": [
    "Bright, clear shallow water near warm coasts, with coral, sea pickles and patches of prismarine in the floor.",
    "",
    "Find a &bPrismarine Reef&r and shear a &aPrismarine Frond&r from between the coral.",
    "",
    "Grafting a Frond here gives Phototrophs, and a Budding Prismarine block placed on a Reef gives Lithophiles, the strain every metal colony comes from.",
  ],
  "quest.2448724FFFA1E08D.quest_desc": [
    "Building on the sea floor goes a lot faster when the sea is out of the way.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aBubble Anchor&r, place it and give it fuel. It holds back every water block in a 15 x 15 x 15 cube around it, so you can walk, mine and build inside in the dry. A ring of bubbles marks the edge.",
    "",
    "A &2Dried Kelp Block&r runs it for two minutes. When the field ends, the sea comes back into every space you did not build in, so wall your room in and set its Ends as button to Air to keep it dry for good.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: a beam of 20 AP or more runs it with no fuel, and a purer beam makes the cube larger, up to 25 blocks across.",
  ],
  "quest.269CCC2DAFB7A9B2.quest_desc": [
    "Iron is the first metal a colony can make for you.",
    "",
    "Mutate &bMetallophiles&r with an Iron Ingot to get &bFerrophiles&r, grow the colony on Iron Ore, and put it to work in a Bio Reactor until it makes its first Iron Ingot.",
    "",
    "A fresh colony makes an ingot every several seconds. Fed Iron Ore from a nutrient slot, it never ages and goes on making ingots for as long as the reactor has power.",
  ],
  "task.296F53A9B893616C.title": "Stacking the Odds",
  "quest.4AEFD35B32DD2489.quest_desc": [
    "Beams carry &bpurity&r as well as power. A catalyst tops out at 1.2, and the better recipes want more.",
    "",
    "Find a &aPrismarine Crystal&r. Every &6Crystal Geode&r, a hollow room buried 10 to 59 blocks under the ocean floor, has one standing in scaffolding in the middle.",
    "",
    "Fire a beam into the crystal's core, the fourth block up from the bottom, from the side. Its top block then fires straight up and its bottom block straight down, both at the full incoming power and purity 3.0. The crystal already stands over the one block gap where you drop items to transform them.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the crystal cannot be moved, so build around it, and keep the catalyst fed. When it stops, every item in the beam starts over.",
  ],
  "quest.3F86B2A1DD7D5AD3.title": "&bAquarine Steel",
  "quest.29CB4422765935BC.title": "&dEldritch Heart",
  "quest.684644505C6D47D4.title": "&5Pressing the Deep",
  "quest.718C50DBF9A20D01.title": "&2Industrial Bio Reactor",
  "quest.49C42EC7FAC6095B.title": "&aRusty Crates",
  "task.47497DC6F8F210A5.title": "Fit a deep fauna augment",
  "quest.3C08268FC890E1A6.title": "&2All in One",
  "task.7B3AB2DCFC601FD7.title": "Automate the output",
  "task.74723EAD9940A6AF.title": "Form and power it",
  "quest.148338A58609D18D.title": "&aLive Catches",
  "quest.55D7BD0D53341399.title": "&bReading the Beam",
  "quest.71F0F2A1ED30A94A.quest_desc": [
    "While you are on an ocean or a river, small patches of open water form near you with glowing spores drifting over them. Those are &blucky zones&r.",
    "",
    "Cast into one with any rod. The bobber holds still, fish bite twice as fast, and each catch adds a roll on the zone's loot table on top of your normal catch.",
    "",
    "A zone lasts five minutes and the first catch uses it up. It only forms where every block around it is open water, so look away from the shore, and each Nautec ocean has its own zone loot.",
  ],
  "quest.589A5835042DC2C1.quest_desc": [
    "Relays only go straight. Optics turn and split a beam, and each one changes its purity on the way through.",
    "",
    "Build one of each and plan your routes around what the machine at the end needs:",
    "",
    "- &aPrismatic Mirror&r: turns a beam through a right angle, out the way you faced when placing it, and keeps nine tenths of the purity.",
    "",
    "- &2Beam Splitter&r: sends one beam out of every side that has a receiver. Power is shared evenly and each output keeps four fifths of the purity.",
    "",
    "- &aFocusing Lens&r: adds 0.5 purity to a beam passing straight through, up to 2.0. A beam already at 2.0 or more comes out unchanged.",
  ],
  "quest.2FB6F345301719AB.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrade multipliers stack by multiplying, so every upgrade raises the cost of all the others.",
    "",
    "In a full Bio Reactor, one Speed and one Yield Upgrade give 3 times the output for 288 AP, the same output two Yield Upgrades give for 324. With nine colonies and four slots, the Industrial Bio Reactor's options are:",
    "",
    "- &bFour Speed&r: 3 times the output for 3,605 AP.",
    "",
    "- &bFour Yield&r: 5 times the output for 5,774 AP.",
    "",
    "- &bTwo Speed, two Yield&r: 6 times the output for 4,562 AP.",
    "",
    "- &bTwo Speed, one Yield, one Efficiency&r: 4 times the output for 3,042 AP, with a quarter less nutrient used per tick.",
    "",
    "Mixing Speed and Yield gives about 50% more items per AP than stacking either one. Add Efficiency only when nutrients run short.",
  ],
  "quest.16B9BE43A2E632A0.title": "&dA Crystal of Your Own",
  "task.197F9B2A9664B4B5.title": "Pipe the output out",
  "task.57EC893BAF9CEF29.title": "&aCultivated Prismarine Crystal",
  "quest.1F00BCA0042DB923.title": "&bGoing With the Current",
  "quest.6F403759246877FB.quest_subtitle": "End of the metal chain",
  "task.2DC0C972539279F1.title": "Redstone and Lapis",
  "quest.3C8951D418D9B9DE.quest_desc": [
    "While you are aboard, anything hunting you attacks the hull instead, and the hull has its own health and diamond-grade armor.",
    "",
    "Keep some &aDeep Steel Plating&r for repairs. A hull that runs out of points throws its crew out unharmed and drops as a breached item that will not launch until you fix it.",
    "",
    "Put the hull in an anvil's left slot and plating in the right. Each plate restores a fifth of the hull for 2 levels. The hull also restores 1% of its points every 10 seconds on its own.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the crew is dropped wherever the hull broke, often deep under water, so keep your diving suit on.",
  ],
  "quest.6C9E2A1AD6F50E3F.quest_desc": [
    "Your first colonies start out on blocks in the world.",
    "",
    "Make a &aGrafting Tool&r, hold it in your main hand with an empty Petri Dish in your off hand, and right-click a block that carries a strain, in the biome it needs. Each try costs one durability and may put a new colony in the dish.",
    "",
    "The tool refuses a dish that already holds a colony, so carry a few empty ones. &eJEI&r's Bacteria Grafting category lists every block, the biome it needs under Only In, and the strain it gives.",
  ],
  "task.1248ABD7B9203F15.title": "Mutation Odds",
  "quest.160787EC65DDE421.title": "&dTapping the Core",
  "quest.4144063FFB1CD735.title": "&aDeep Sea Drain",
  "quest.6A82B052670383C2.quest_desc": [
    "A Resonance Pylon cannot reach another dimension. An &aAbyssal Pylon&r can.",
    "",
    "It joins the same networks, moves 50,000 FE/t and holds 500,000 FE. Power sent between dimensions loses 15%, and only travels from one Abyssal Pylon to another.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: it needs a Nether Star, so plan a Wither fight before you build one.",
  ],
  "quest.237CBF1B089BC523.title": "&aCast Iron",
  "quest.5085CFD8AB65A4B3.title": "&aTidal Power",
  "quest.5E3EDE7F8AF2489A.quest_desc": [
    "Armored Vent Crawlers walk the floor of the Hydrothermal Vents. They run when hurt, shrug off half of any knockback and take no fire damage.",
    "",
    "Chase one down for its &aChitin Plates&r. Each drops one to three, more with Looting.",
    "",
    "Four plates make the &dVent Carapace&r augment, one in each of the Augmentation Station's four extensions, and the Sea Scout's Armour Module takes one.",
  ],
  "quest.25F78E2C1065E392.title": "&2Adamantophiles",
  "task.524EEFBF846BE1E7.title": "&eObserve&r: Gateway",
  "quest.0C52C98FB27EA46F.title": "&bLantern Jellies",
  "quest.31895972F81D14AE.quest_desc": [
    "Running cables across a seabed base gets old fast.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aResonance Pylon&r. Right-click it with an empty hand to name a network, then set each pylon to Sending or Receiving. FE goes in or out on any side, and every pylon on the network shares it.",
    "",
    "A pylon moves up to 20,000 FE/t and loses 5% on the way, between pylons in the same dimension. Turn on Load in a pylon's screen and it keeps its own chunk loaded, so a far-off end keeps working while nobody is there.",
    "",
    "You can own up to 16 networks, and each one can be shared with a trusted player or your FTB Team.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Resonance Network\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:deep_engineering/resonance_network.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.4FB344B1F965D434.title": "&3Piloting",
  "quest.5060BFECF1EE9856.quest_desc": [
    "The wild rings only go where they were built. A crafted one goes where you send it.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aGateway&r. It comes packed with its whole ring, so placing it builds the 13 block ring at once, standing across the way you face with its front toward you.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "",
    "The opening is 9 blocks across, wide enough to steer a &2Sea Scout&r straight through. Anything that passes through comes out of the front of the nearest other ring with the same address, still moving at the same speed.",
    "",
    "Sneak and right-click the ring with any wrench to pack it back into one item, address included. That is also how you carry a wild ring home. Mining a formed ring takes as long as obsidian by hand and drops nothing.",
  ],
  "quest.2AC4B42D14073C81.title": "&dHarvest Time",
  "quest.027581A4ED726B8B.title": "&aAquarine Steel Tools",
  "quest.4FB344B1F965D434.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\", {\"keybind\": \"key.forward\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: W\"}}, \" and \", {\"keybind\": \"key.back\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: S\"}}, \" work the throttle, \", {\"keybind\": \"key.jump\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: Space\"}}, \" rises and \", {\"keybind\": \"key.nautec.submarine_descend\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: C\"}}, \" dives. There is no turn key, because the hull follows where you look.\"]",
    "",
    "Hold right-click to look around without steering, and let go to snap back to the nose. The hull refuses to turn into rock rather than clip through it, and on the surface its thrusters work at about a third of their strength. Sneaking always climbs out.",
    "",
    "An empty hull keeps its charge. With someone aboard, sitting still costs 1 power per tick, moving 6 more and keeping the crew breathing 2 more. When the cell runs flat the seal goes with it, so surface or dock before then.",
  ],
  "quest.3787C51DB72BF43D.title": "&5Pressure Synthesizer",
  "quest.0C52C98FB27EA46F.quest_desc": [
    "Lantern Jellies drift slowly through the Bioluminescent Grove, glowing as they go. They are passive and have little health.",
    "",
    "Hunt one for its &aLuminous Membrane&r. Each drops one or two, more with Looting.",
    "",
    "The membrane becomes the &dPhotophore Skin&r augment, and the Sea Scout's Stealth Module needs some too.",
  ],
  "quest.3EE21DDC41B24798.title": "&dDeep Fauna Augments",
  "quest.5085FC6585F588B9.title": "&2Mutation Odds",
  "quest.24C3B87362113EA7.quest_desc": [
    "The bigger biology machines all start with &aBacteria Containment Shields&r.",
    "",
    "Make at least two for the Mutator. The Fuel Cell takes one more, and a Bio Reactor's frame needs another eight.",
    "",
    "Crafting them around a &2Prismarine Crystal Shard&r gives four at a time instead of two.",
  ],
  "quest.12FC9636258A86B5.title": "&bBioluminescent Grove",
  "quest.674023982F732B18.title": "&dAwakening",
  "quest.2C61275C9E6B6CF8.quest_desc": [
    "Copper on its own is too soft for pipework under the sea. A crystal beam hardens it into something you can build with.",
    "",
    "Craft Aquarine Copper Compound and drop it into a beam with a purity of 2.1 or more to get &aAquarine Copper Ingots&r, four from each compound. A &2Focusing Lens&r stops at 2.0, so fire the beam through a &2Prismarine Crystal&r first.",
    "",
    "The &2Mixer&r makes the compound in bulk, turning three Copper Ingots, a Kelp Slurry and 500 mB of Salt Water into six.",
  ],
  "quest.67073110A3FA00CB.quest_desc": [
    "You cannot build much on the sea floor on one lungful of air.",
    "",
    "Make all four pieces of the &aDiving Suit&r. With the full set on, the chestplate's tank keeps your breath topped up under water for up to ten minutes.",
    "",
    "A new chestplate comes with a full tank. Drink a Pressurized Air Bottle while wearing it for two more minutes, and fill Glass Bottles at any bubble column to make more. The full suit also keeps you breathing in space on &eStellaris&r planets.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the helmet clears underwater fog even on its own.",
  ],
  "task.74F87726661A6E3B.title": "&eObserve&r: Gateway Ring",
  "quest.3D2B05F88D95FA3C.title": "&bFollow the Pearl",
  "quest.07DB72267839D8D7.quest_desc": [
    "Two modules get you out of trouble.",
    "",
    "Fit a &aBooster Module&r for 10 seconds of 45% more thrust, and a &2Stealth Module&r that makes every creature within 32 blocks lose track of the hull for two minutes.",
    "",
    "Stealth costs 15% of your thrust while it runs. Fire the Booster alongside it and the two together leave you a little faster than normal.",
  ],
  "quest.6BE0A49FD008FB92.title": "&dThe Cradle",
  "quest.6351729D4F3ED437.title": "&dOrgans From the Sea",
  "quest.67073110A3FA00CB.title": "&bDiving Gear",
  "quest.66E132073DA81E4A.title": "&aSilt Skippers",
  "quest.2112D4B209CCCE84.quest_subtitle": "Thousands of ingots a minute",
  "quest.6C51CE5E6702F34F.title": "&2Other Mods' Metals",
  "quest.0EEFEF7693B5FC78.title": "&5Doing Time",
  "quest.3BA1F3D850C3C624.title": "&dEye in the Sky",
  "quest.1485B05D33FAFFE5.title": "&bPrismarine Crystal Shards",
  "quest.6BE0A49FD008FB92.quest_desc": [
    "Place a &aCrystal Cradle&r with six blocks of air or water above it, then right-click it with the awakened seed.",
    "",
    "Fire beams of purity 2.0 or more into any of its four sides. All of their AP goes into growth, and the seed becomes a crystal at 10,000,000 AP: about 83 minutes at 100 AP/t, or 8 minutes at 1,000 AP/t.",
    "",
    "Growth is never lost. Break the cradle and it keeps both the seed and its progress.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Open the \", {\"text\": \"Crystal Cultivation\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nautec:guide,nautec:deep_engineering/crystal_cultivation.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Nautec Guide\"}}, \" page in the Nautec Guide.\"]",
  ],
  "task.4F2C0B61A7634EA7.title": "Surface Strains",
  "quest.60D72BA4EEBEF0EF.quest_desc": [
    "Grafting only gets you a handful of strains. Everything else comes from mutation.",
    "",
    "Build a &aMutator&r and power it with at least 10 AP into its top or bottom. Put a colony in the left slot and the catalyst in the item slot, and every 12 seconds it makes an attempt until one succeeds. ",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The catalyst is never used up, and the right slot has to be empty before it starts. &eJEI&r's Bacteria Mutations category lists every catalyst and its base chance.",
    "",
    "On a success the new strain starts at its own starting size and carries the parent's stats forward with a small random shift. Mutation is the only thing that ever changes a colony's stats.",
  ],
  "quest.2112D4B209CCCE84.title": "&2Mass Production",
  "quest.46E756E1EDEF8DE0.title": "&2Carbophages",
  "quest.675D7B6F6826316D.title": "&aSalt Water",
  "quest.2C30458D324A4AD9.title": "&2Metallophiles",
  "quest.63177C0A3FA7720F.title": "&3Teleport Module",
  "quest.36E74E70F0ACCAD5.title": "&2Nine at Once",
  "quest.2DD115082017F9E3.title": "&bCharger and Battery",
  "quest.4702ABE2F7F6FD31.quest_desc": [
    "Each working colony eats about one nutrient a minute, and a big farm goes through a lot of ore.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aReactor Efficiency Upgrade&r for when nutrients, not power, are what runs short. Each one cuts the nutrient buffer a colony spends by a quarter and multiplies the power draw by 1.2.",
    "",
    "The cuts multiply, so one leaves 75%, two 56% and four 32%. A nutrient that lasts a minute then stretches to 80 seconds of work with one and 190 with four, and items come out no faster or slower.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Like the others, it needs parts from \", {\"text\": \"Pressing the Deep\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"684644505C6D47D4\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to Pressing the Deep Quest\"}}, \".\"]",
  ],
}